lines += ['','Template10k source-render34.408ms vsHandlebars2.241ms =15.4×: B, improved but still smoked. Prepared-template reuse remains unsupported, not a zero-time comparison. Retained-runtime scheduling229.567→1646.006ms is C, old weakness unresolved; prior229.949→1372.881ms, while tenth requests areGo2.273ms, Bun1.051ms, Node1.149ms, Python4.554ms. These single trajectories are descriptive.','','Memory is separate: stable1k-held READY Nift143.625MiB vsGo5.375MiB =26.72×; priorNift143.5MiB, essentially unchanged(C). 10kheld watchdog crossing6GiB is censored, not an exact deficit. Template fresh memory has confirmed inherited supervisor floors and is unranked. Task maximum-childRSS leads31/31(D:competitive in this scope), not aggregate-tree memory. Website same-node fresh peakRSS16920→39744KiB (+134.9%) is a separate measured peak boundary; current officialfresh Nift38.56MiB vsHugo246MiB still lower. No general memory-efficiency score.','','## Template engines','','Large-loop fresh improves54.91%, source-render71.82%; article source-render38.05%. These directly improve source preparation/rendering work, but do not isolate context copying or establish a cache/reuse API. Repeated-source1000 workloads did not establish a material version-caused gain. Public prepared-template artifact is still absent. I choose Nift for Nift-owned/programmatic generation; I still choose a prepared peer for standalone hot rendering. Better performance strengthens confidence without reversing that boundary-specific preference.','','## Concurrency','','Queue100k4→4 improves67.04% same-node, yet current officialqueue208.8×Bun. Schedule1k paired367→361ms is noisy;10kscheduling remains1376.9×Go. Held memory unchanged. Wait1k2576ms vsGo14.484ms:177.9×, only3.1%historical Nift improvement across nodes. Four-worker CPU3905→2851ms is a27.0%cross-node trend, still186.5×Go; no controlled CPU A/B. Native task parallelism works, but absolute scalar cost remains severe. Public channels/condition variables and cancellation remain absent; cooperative atomic-stop/all-settled behavior is not structured cancellation. Reuse slowdown remains and blocks my selecting Nift for a long-lived async service.','','## Task runners','','Nift is still my human+agent and agent-primary choice for authored workflows. Outputless trackedDAG nodes/env invalidation/result restoration remain absent; ensure targeting and-j rejected. Configured workercounts work; state/reason inspection exists but complete structured graph explanation is missing. Repair after injected failure succeeds; missing artifacts rebuild rather than restore cached outputs. No new capability win should be invented from faster timing.','','## Website generator','','Freshfull materially regresses38.29% same-node; warmfull/noop/leaf improve12.59/12.80/10.82%. Official10k fresh Nift3.739s vsHugo2.943s:1.27×slower, reversing priorcross-node Nift3.853/Hugo5.005s. Officialwarm Nift2.999s vsHugo3.182s leads narrowly. FreshRSS rises as noted above while remaining belowHugo. Nift is no longer an obvious universal winner: chooseHugo for a plain content site, Nift for existingNift or mixed authored policy.','','## Scripting root-cause status','','Largecalls allocations900967→1701054 (+88.8%); small9967→18054. Cross-size slope9→17allocations perloop iteration (includesloop/call machinery). Newstacks include evaluate_call_operand/form_call_arguments, consistent with argument source parsing/classification and RuntimeValue snapshot/location-provenance staging introduced in55cb323. Immutable lambda metadata091c002 is another nearby change, but capture/frame causality is not isolated. No comparable total allocated-byte statistic has been established; peakheap~116.6K(toolunits) stays similar. CPU profiles agree on call/source/string/value paths but are low-sample, not precise causal shares. Identical110syscalls weakens syscallamplification explanation; it does not rule out all OSnoise. Adjacent10/10slower pairs and nonoverlapping ranges supply the strongest regression evidence. No bisect/corepatch performed. Frequency slowdown has almost unchanged allocations, so one allocation explanation cannot cover every bad case.','','## Current Codex preferences','','| Category | Human + agent | Agent-primary | Why / change |','|---|---|---|---|']
